{"afterMs":300,"event":{"type":"agent.text.delta","payload":{"sessionId":"$SESSION","messageId":"$MSG","delta":"\n\n## Your Japan trip cost about €3,700\n\nI reconciled the Studio Northstar travel-agency contract against your booking confirmations and both bank statements for **11–22 April 2026** (Tokyo + Kyoto).\n\n### Package booked through Studio Northstar — ≈ €3,150\n- Flights (LHR–HND–LHR): **€985.00**\n- Tokyo Riverside Hotel, 6 nights: **¥168,000**\n- Kyoto Ryokan Sakura, 3 nights: **¥96,000**\n- 7-day JR rail pass: **¥50,000**\n- Two guided day tours: **¥38,000**\n- Agency service fee: **€120.00**\n\nThe contract pegs the package at **~€3,150**, and the charges match: **€1,105** on your EUR travel card (flights + fee) and **¥352,000** on your JPY account (hotel, ryokan, rail, tours).\n\n### On-the-ground spending — ≈ €557\n- Sushi Aoyama omakase: ¥28,000\n- Hanami Tei kaiseki: ¥22,000\n- teamLab Planets (×2): ¥4,800\n- Uniqlo Ginza: ¥9,800\n- Don Quijote souvenirs: ¥7,400\n- Tokyo Metro & konbini: ¥6,200\n- Tokyo Bay Ramen + Haneda meal: €102.20\n\n### Total: ≈ **€3,707**\nThat's the €3,150 Studio Northstar package plus ≈ €557 of dining, activities and shopping on the ground. Your single biggest line was the Tokyo hotel (¥168,000 ≈ €975). Everything ties out: every booking confirmation has a matching bank charge."}}}
